.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Bobcat_tracks_in_mud.jpg/500px-Bobcat_tracks_in_mud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bobcat tracks in mud showing the hindpaw print (top) partially covering the forepaw print (center)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABobcat_tracks_in_mud.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Bobcatonwires.jpg/500px-Bobcatonwires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Bobcatonwires.jpg/1280px-Bobcatonwires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Bobcatonwires.jpg/500px-Bobcatonwires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bobcat climbing on a utility pole at the Kennedy Space Center in Florida. The species' range does not seem to be limited by human populations, as long as it can still find a suitable habitat.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABobcatonwires.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Calero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg/500px-Calero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Calero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg/1280px-Calero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Calero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg/500px-Calero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bobcat spotted in South San Jose, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalero_Creek_Trail_Bobcat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w